.TH IBNETLENS 1 "2026" "ibnetlens 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ibnetlens \- parse, validate and convert InfiniBand topology files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ibnetlens
[\fBparse\fR] [\fB\-F\fR \fIformat\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fItext\fR] [\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR|\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-stats\fR] \fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR
.br
.B ibnetlens check
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] \fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR
.br
.B ibnetlens diff
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] \fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR
.br
.B ibnetlens info
[\fB\-q\fR] \fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the topology file written by
.BR ibnetdiscover (8)
(or standard input when the file is \fB\-\fR) and converts it, checks it for inconsistencies or compares it with a later snapshot.
The free-form net files read by
.BR ibsim (1)
and the topology files written by NVIDIA ibdiagnet (with port labels in parentheses) are accepted as well.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B parse
Convert the topology to another format. This is the default command.
.TP
.B check
Report duplicate GUIDs and LIDs, links without a matching reverse entry, links whose peer reports a different remote port, mismatched or degraded link speeds, and links to nodes absent from the file.
.TP
.B diff
List nodes and links added, removed or changed between two files.
.TP
.B info
Print node, link and speed counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-format " \fIformat\fR"
One of json (default), csv (links), csv\-nodes, dot, slurm, ibnd, legacy.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Write to \fIfile\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " text"
With the slurm format, skip adapters whose description contains \fItext\fR.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Use \fIN\fR threads. By default the count is chosen from the input size and the number of CPUs.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Stop with status 2 on the first malformed line instead of warning and continuing.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress parser warnings. Also hides the progress bar unless \fB\-\-progress\fR is given.
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Show parse progress on standard error. By default progress is shown only when standard error is a terminal; a bar appears after a short delay and is erased when parsing ends. When forced on a non-terminal, one line is printed per 10%.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Never show progress. Use this in scripts and cron jobs. The last of \fB\-\-progress\fR and \fB\-\-no\-progress\fR wins.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print phase times, peak memory, thread count and node and port counts to standard error as one key=value line.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit check or diff results as one JSON object per line.
.SH SLURM OUTPUT
A switch with at least as many hosts as links to other switches is a leaf and becomes a Nodes= line; every other switch lists the switches one level below it in Switches=. A spine that also serves hosts gets a synthetic leaf named after it with the suffix h. Host names are the first word of the adapter description.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when check or diff found something, 2 on usage or input errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ibnetdiscover (8)
